@page "/components/growth-business"

<PageTitle>Growth Business — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Growth Business</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    ui-layouts' "grow business" pricing section, ported class for class: three plan cards on a
    slate canvas, a lime monthly/yearly switch, prices that roll digit by digit when it flips, and
    every piece sharpening in out of a blur the first time the section is scrolled to.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">As it ships</h2>
<Example Source="GrowthBusinessExample.razor" Block><GrowthBusinessExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Your own plans</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Plans</code> takes <code>PricingTier(Name, Description, MonthlyPrice, YearlyPrice,
    Features)</code> records; <code>Featured</code> makes the dark card and <code>Href</code>
    makes its button a link. The switch is a real checkbox and every price is in the markup twice,
    so it works with scripting off; the roll is the only part that needs a script.
</p>
<Example Source="GrowthBusinessCustom.razor" Block><GrowthBusinessCustom /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">A fixed, light palette</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Upstream draws this section in slate, neutral and lime with no dark variant, and so does the
    port: on a dark page it stays a light section. Wrap it, or pass <code>Class</code>, to change
    the canvas.
</p>
